Captured on Knowhere (ASUS TUF Gaming A14 FA401EA, AMD Ryzen AI MAX+ 392,
CachyOS) on 2026-10-15 with tests/fixtures/capture-linux.sh, as a normal
user. No serial numbers, UUIDs or battery manufacturer/model strings.

The telemetry files (hwmon temperatures, cpufreq/scaling_cur_freq and the
ACPI platform profile) were added on 2026-10-18 from a capture with the
extended script, without changing the files captured before.

run/udev/data/+dmi:id (added 2026-10-20): the SMBIOS memory devices
(type 17) from Dave's `dmidecode -t 17` on Knowhere, serials and asset
tags removed, written in systemd's dmi_memory_id spellings with the
capture script's whitelisted fields (it is not a udev capture: the
values are dmidecode's). 8 soldered LPDDR5 devices, "DIMM 0" in
"P0 CHANNEL A" .. "P0 CHANNEL H", 4 GiB, 32-bit each, Form Factor
"Other", 1R, rated 8,532 MT/s, configured 8,000 MT/s, Micron
(Bank 1, 0x2C) MT62F1G32D2DS-023 WT.
